# Expectation record for 01_integer_conversions/006_char_signedness_explicit.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 006_char_signedness_explicit
area               = 01_integer_conversions
description        = Explicit signed char and unsigned char conversions and arithmetic, folded and volatile-runtime
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Plain char is never used for a signedness-dependent value.  Every character object is
spelled signed char or unsigned char, so its range is fixed by the program rather than by
the implementation.  Each signed value stays inside the destination range, unsigned
results wrap modularly as defined, and every shift count is in range.
Every property is computed twice, once from literal constants and once from
volatile-qualified storage, so the constant folder's answer cannot stand in for the
one the backend computes at run time.
No header is included and printf is declared by hand, so nothing here depends on a
standard-library header bcc does not ship.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
Plain char has implementation-defined signedness and was measured signed on x86-64 and
i686 but unsigned on AArch64 and RISC-V 64.  Rather than restrict the target list, the
program removes the dependence entirely by never using plain char for a value whose
signedness matters, so all four targets remain fully compared and nothing is excluded.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
fold_schar_min=-128
fold_schar_max=127
fold_uchar_max=255
fold_schar_to_uchar=255
fold_uchar_to_schar=-56
fold_int_to_schar=-56
fold_int_to_uchar=255
fold_uchar_add=256
fold_schar_sub=-129
fold_schar_shift=-1
fold_uchar_shift=100
fold_schar_uchar_diff=0
run_schar_min=-128
run_schar_max=127
run_uchar_max=255
run_schar_to_uchar=255
run_uchar_to_schar=-56
run_int_to_schar=-56
run_int_to_uchar=255
run_uchar_add=256
run_schar_sub=-129
run_schar_shift=-1
run_uchar_shift=100
run_schar_uchar_diff=0
schar_promotes=int
uchar_promotes=int
END
